<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>DiagnosticCatalog.PublicApi</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>DiagnosticCatalog.PublicApi</RootNamespace>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    This catalogue ships on the 'publicapi' train, which versions independently of the foundation so
    it can follow Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers' releases without dragging anything else
    along. Declaring the train here is the whole membership (Directory.Build.targets); it is also
    what makes the project packable, what gives it an embedded SBOM, and what puts the icon on the
    package.

    A train of its own rather than sharing 'roslyn'. The two packages ship from the same repository
    and version in lockstep today, but they are separate NuGet packages a consumer installs
    separately, and one of them is an opt-in a library chooses while the other arrives transitively.
    Sharing a train would tie a release of either to the other's changelog.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ReleaseTrain>publicapi</ReleaseTrain>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>DiagnosticCatalog.PublicApi</PackageId>
    <DevelopmentDependency>false</DevelopmentDependency>
    <Title>DiagnosticCatalog.PublicApi</Title>
    <Description>The public-API tracking rules (RS00xx) as strongly referenced constants, so that SuppressMessageAttribute takes compile-checked references instead of magic strings. Ids, categories, titles and help links are read from Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers' own DiagnosticDescriptor instances. For any library tracking its surface in PublicAPI.Shipped.txt. Unofficial; not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft.</Description>
    <PackageTags>roslyn;analyzers;diagnostics;suppressmessage;publicapi;api-tracking;api-compatibility;code-analysis;catalog</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.en.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Authors>Reefact</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Reefact</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Reefact/diagnostic-catalog</PackageProjectUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    A PACKAGE reference, not a project one. The foundation rides the 'lib' train and this catalogue
    rides its own, so packing against the project would stamp a dependency on a lib version that was
    never published, and every consumer's restore would fail with NU1102 on an immutable artifact
    (ADR-0007).

    Version-less, so it resolves from Directory.Packages.props — where moving every catalogue onto a
    new foundation is one deliberate edit rather than twelve.

    NOT PrivateAssets="all": the foundation must reach whoever consumes this catalogue. They need
    [DiagnosticRule] resolvable to declare rules of their own, and present at run time for reflection
    over a catalogue to work (specification §16.1).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="DiagnosticCatalog" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.en.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
